  "pulses_per_direction": 9,
  "purpose": "controlled response probe for traversability, second run, placed on the cells where the route B v15 mask actually makes its decision. The first run (active-probe-v26) established the estimator, the acceptance rule and the idle separation on hardware but sat about 22 to 24 px east of the stall cell 14:11, so it measured a different region and found nothing blocked. This version raises the repeats from three to nine per direction because the first run spread twenty-four pulses over fourteen cells and only four of nineteen cell-bearing pairs reached the sample floor, and it declares a containment region around the target cluster so a session that wanders away from it fails instead of silently measuring somewhere else. The question is unchanged and specific: in cell 14:11 the incidental grid removed north with the largest sample count in the whole grid (n=125, rate 0.071 against 0.187-0.325 baseline) while north-east in the same cell measured 0.304, and a declared, drift-controlled, direction-balanced schedule has to say whether north is structurally dead there.",
